{
 "title": "First-passage horizons in HVG rank-invariant estimator of path roughness - replication spec",
 "hypothesis": "theta(H)=1-H for fBm integer-grid persistence Molchan 1999 and conditional on RL-fBm increment hypothesis Eq hyp-rl for rough Bergomi; exact uncensored Lp=Tp Lemma and i.i.d. null P[Lp>=k]=1/k Prop Renyi record.",
 "data_sources": [
  "Monte Carlo: fBm, rough Bergomi, Heston, GARCH, FIGARCH simulated via authors code from paper description",
  "Real: FRED VIXCLS daily CBOE VIX 2000-01-03 to 2026-04-30 via FRED API"
 ],
 "sample": "FRED daily CBOE VIX (VIXCLS) 2000-01-03 to 2026-04-30 n=6651 trading days, no licence filter. Rolling estimator W=1024 days (~4y) step 126 days (~6m) =45 windows. Synthetic validation: fBm Davies-Harte T=2^16 per path, N per H cell; rough Bergomi hybrid kappa=1 xi0=0.04, H x eta grid; control processes T=2^16; empirical i.i.d. null W=512..65536 with N=1000/500 replicates; overlapping-window i.i.d. null 1000 paths length 6651.",
 "period_start": "2000-01-03",
 "period_end": "2026-04-30",
 "method": [
  "1. For path x[1..T] with no ties compute forward visibility horizon Lp(t)=sup{k>=1:(t,t+k) in HVG, x[t+k]>=x[t]} = Tp(t)=inf{k>=1:x[t+k]>=x[t]} by monotone stack next-greater-or-equal O(T). If set empty before T, observation at t is right-censored, not assigned value. Deterministic time-order tie break: x[t+k]==x[t] counts as crossing; sensitivity checked with stricter convention.",
  "2. Main estimate complete-case on uncensored Lp: L=(Lp(t_i)) i=1..n <=T-1. Hill-MLE theta_hat(l0)=n_l0 / sum_{L_i>=l0} log(L_i/l0), n_l0=#{L_i>=l0}. Asymptotic SE theta_hat/sqrt(n_l0) replaced by stationary block bootstrap Politis-Romano 1994 with mean block b=ceil(T^{1/3}), B=200 resamples.",
  "3. Threshold l0* by Clauset-Shalizi-Newman 2009: for each candidate integer l0 compute theta_hat(l0) and KS distance between empirical tail of L above l0 and Pareto(theta_hat(l0)). Minimiser = l0*. Candidate set = integers 1..min(19,floor(q0.9)) plus 30 log-spaced integers 20..q0.9 with duplicates removed, q0.9=empirical 90% quantile.",
  "4. Censoring sensitivity at l0*: censored Pareto likelihood theta_cens=n_u/[sum_u log(L_i/l0*)+sum_c log(C_j/l0*)] and lower-bound fit treating C_j as exact, u=uncensored, c=censored tail.",
  "5. fBm validation: Davies-Harte for H=0.1..0.9 N=10000 T=2^16 each; control processes T=2^16 N=50; rough Bergomi Eq.v_t=xi0 exp(eta Z^H_t -0.5 eta^2 t^{2H}) RL-fBm hybrid kappa=1; model comparison rough Bergomi H0.1, Heston, GARCH(1,1), FIGARCH(1,d,1) N=10000 T=2^16; heatmap H=0.05,0.10,0.15,0.20,0.30 x eta=0.2,0.4 N=10000 per cell.",
  "6. VIX rolling: Hill-CSN per 1024-day window step 126. Single-window i.i.d. null N=1000 uniform length 1024; overlapping-window i.i.d. null 1000 paths length 6651 with same rolling scheme. Count windows with theta_hat <2.5% null quantile and rolling mean vs null mean, Monte-Carlo p with add-one smoothing."
 ],
